policy 1→2: 4 deprecation warnings spanning 2 operations; assert code set is unique → ["WARN_DEPRECATED_FIELD"], fieldPaths set {legacyCode, holder.phone} per each op. Assert findings.every(code WARN_DEPRECATED_FIELD) and the sorted unique fieldPaths.

claims: amountApproved across 2 operations (POST 201 + GET 200) → 2 NOW_OPTIONAL; assert that all fieldPath is amountApproved and that both GET and POST operations are covered? In the matrix, mobile-app reads GET. Assert that unique fieldPaths = [amountApproved], all codes NOW_OPTIONAL.

Also, does GET /quotes/{quoteId} share `documents`? No, that's claims. claims POST 201 Claim → yes amountApproved is there too.

Add an alias test: collectParamAliases for quote 1→2 returns {id→quoteId}.

Update the test file accordingly.

